<sup><b>1</b></sup> Lord, who shall abide in thy tabernacle? who shall dwell in thy holy hill?<br />
<sup><b>2</b></sup> He that walketh uprightly, and worketh righteousness, and speaketh the truth in his heart.<br />
<sup><b>3</b></sup> <i>He that</i> backbiteth not with his tongue, nor doeth evil to his neighbour, nor taketh up a reproach against his neighbour.<br />
<sup><b>4</b></sup> In whose eyes a vile person is contemned; but he honoureth them that fear the Lord. <i>He that</i> sweareth to <i>his own</i> hurt, and changeth not.<br />
<sup><b>5</b></sup> <i>He that</i> putteth not out his money to usury, nor taketh reward against the innocent. He that doeth these <i>things</i> shall never be moved. <br />
